        "locator": "PubMed abstract: experiments compare effects of perceptual load with working-memory or dual-task coordination load on distractor interference."
      },
      {
        "span_id": "s2",
        "locator": "PubMed abstract: high perceptual load reduces distractor interference, whereas memory/coordination load increases it."
      },
      {
        "span_id": "s3",
        "locator": "PubMed abstract: the pattern is interpreted as two mechanisms, one limiting distractor perception under high perceptual demand and another maintaining task priorities when control resources are available."
      }
